IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc26-interpretation`

-- ccc26-principles.l4 -- sections 718 to 718.21 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the purpose and principles of sentencing
-- (lines 15190-15250 of the text). Layer 1 of part ccc26. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws
-- Website consolidation; it is not the official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The directions in these sections are addressed to the court. Each is encoded for what it decides for the person sentenced:
-- the open-textured judgments the text leaves to the court (proportionate, similar, unduly harsh, vulnerable) are plain inputs.

§ `Section 718 -- Purpose: the objectives of sentencing`

-- The purpose statement ("to protect society ... by imposing just sanctions") creates no rule of its own; the objectives it lists are
-- named here because sections 718.01 to 718.07 give two of them primary consideration.
-- src:15190 | Purpose and Principles of Sentencing
-- src:15191 | Purpose
-- src:15192 | 718 The fundamental purpose of sentencing is to protect society and to contribute, along with crime prevention initiatives, to respect for the law and the maintenance of a just, peaceful and safe society by imposing just sanctions that have one or more of the following objectives:
-- src:15193 | (a) to denounce unlawful conduct and the harm done to victims or to the community that is caused by unlawful conduct;
-- src:15194 | (b) to deter the offender and other persons from committing offences;
-- src:15195 | (c) to separate offenders from society, where necessary;
-- src:15196 | (d) to assist in rehabilitating offenders;
-- src:15197 | (e) to provide reparations for harm done to victims or to the community; and
-- src:15198 | (f) to promote a sense of responsibility in offenders, and acknowledgment of the harm done to victims or to the community.
@ref s 718 (src:15190-15198)
DECLARE `s 718 objective of sentencing` IS ONE OF
    `s 718(a) denunciation of unlawful conduct and of the harm done to victims or to the community`
    `s 718(b) deterrence of the offender and of other persons`
    `s 718(c) separation of offenders from society, where necessary`
    `s 718(d) rehabilitation of offenders`
    `s 718(e) reparations for harm done to victims or to the community`
    `s 718(f) promotion of a sense of responsibility in offenders, and acknowledgment of the harm done`

@ref s 718 (src:15192-15198)
GIVEN `the objectives the sanction has` IS A LIST OF `s 718 objective of sentencing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718 the sanction has one or more of the objectives the section lists` MEANS
    IF NOT (null `the objectives the sanction has`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section says what just sanctions are imposed to achieve; it does not say that a sanction with none of the six is not a just sanction

§ `Sections 718.01 to 718.07 -- primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence`

-- Each is a direction to the court that, when the offence is of the kind named, denunciation (718(a)) and deterrence (718(b)) come first.
-- The function is the provision's own question: does this section require primary consideration here? The "when" and "if" gates are
-- the text's own (ruling on "when", "upon" and "whenever" counting as "where": JUST FALSE where the gate fails).

-- src:15199 | Objectives — offences against children
-- src:15200 | 718.01 When a court imposes a sentence for an offence that involved the abuse of a person under the age of eighteen years, it shall give primary consideration to the objectives of denunciation and deterrence of such conduct.
@ref s 718.01 (src:15199-15200)
GIVEN `the offence involved the abuse of a person under the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.01 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    IF `the offence involved the abuse of a person under the age of eighteen years`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a court imposes a sentence for an offence that involved the abuse of a person under the age of eighteen years"

-- The two objectives that sections 718.01 to 718.07 give primary consideration to.
@ref s 718.01 (src:15200)
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 718 objective of sentencing`
`s 718.01 the objectives given primary consideration` MEANS
    LIST `s 718(a) denunciation of unlawful conduct and of the harm done to victims or to the community`,
         `s 718(b) deterrence of the offender and of other persons`

-- src:15201 | Objectives — offence against peace officer or other justice system participant
-- src:15202 | 718.02 When a court imposes a sentence for an offence under subsection 270(1), section 270.01 or 270.02 or paragraph 423.1(1)(b), the court shall give primary consideration to the objectives of denunciation and deterrence of the conduct that forms the basis of the offence.
@ref s 718.02 (src:15201-15202)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    IF    (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 270 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
       OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 270.01
       OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 270.02
       OR (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 423.1 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)(b)")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a court imposes a sentence for an offence under subsection 270(1), section 270.01 or 270.02 or paragraph 423.1(1)(b)"

-- src:15203 | Objectives — offence against certain animals
-- src:15204 | 718.03 When a court imposes a sentence for an offence under subsection 445.01(1), the court shall give primary consideration to the objectives of denunciation and deterrence of the conduct that forms the basis of the offence.
@ref s 718.03 (src:15203-15204)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.03 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    IF `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 445.01 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a court imposes a sentence for an offence under subsection 445.01(1)"

-- src:15205 | Objectives — offence against vulnerable person
-- src:15206 | 718.04 When a court imposes a sentence for an offence that involved the abuse of a person who is vulnerable because of personal circumstances — including because the person is Aboriginal and female — the court shall give primary consideration to the objectives of denunciation and deterrence of the conduct that forms the basis of the offence.
@ref s 718.04 (src:15205-15206)
GIVEN `the offence involved the abuse of a person who is vulnerable because of personal circumstances, including because the person is Aboriginal and female` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.04 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    IF `the offence involved the abuse of a person who is vulnerable because of personal circumstances, including because the person is Aboriginal and female`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a court imposes a sentence for an offence that involved the abuse of a person who is vulnerable because of personal circumstances"

-- src:15207 | Objectives — offence of motor vehicle theft when violence used
-- src:15208 | 718.05 If a court imposes a sentence for a second or subsequent offence under subsection 333.1(3), it shall give primary consideration to the objectives of denunciation and deterrence of the conduct that forms the basis of the offence.
@ref s 718.05 (src:15207-15208)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.05 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    IF     `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 333.1 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"
       AND `the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a court imposes a sentence for a second or subsequent offence under subsection 333.1(3)"

-- src:15209 | Objectives — offence of breaking and entering
-- src:15210 | 718.06 If a court imposes a sentence for a second or subsequent offence under section 348, it shall give primary consideration to the objectives of denunciation and deterrence of the conduct that forms the basis of the offence.
@ref s 718.06 (src:15209-15210)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.06 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    IF     `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 348
       AND `the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a court imposes a sentence for a second or subsequent offence under section 348"

-- src:15211 | Objectives — offence for the benefit of a criminal organization
-- src:15212 | 718.07 If a court imposes a sentence for an offence that is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, it shall give primary consideration to the objectives of denunciation and deterrence of the conduct that forms the basis of the offence.
@ref s 718.07 (src:15211-15212)
GIVEN `the offence was committed for the benefit of a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence was committed at the direction of a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence was committed in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.07 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    IF    `the offence was committed for the benefit of a criminal organization`
       OR `the offence was committed at the direction of a criminal organization`
       OR `the offence was committed in association with a criminal organization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a court imposes a sentence for an offence that is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization"

§ `Section 718.1 -- Fundamental principle: proportionality`

-- src:15213 | Fundamental principle
-- src:15214 | 718.1 A sentence must be proportionate to the gravity of the offence and the degree of responsibility of the offender.
@ref s 718.1 (src:15213-15214)
GIVEN `the sentence is proportionate to the gravity of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sentence is proportionate to the degree of responsibility of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.1 the sentence is proportionate` MEANS
    IF `the sentence is proportionate to the gravity of the offence` AND `the sentence is proportionate to the degree of responsibility of the offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sentence must be proportionate to the gravity of the offence and the degree of responsibility of the offender"

§ `Section 718.2 -- Other sentencing principles`

-- Lead-in: "A court that imposes a sentence shall also take into consideration the following principles". The relative clause is a scope
-- limit with no "only", so a court that is not imposing a sentence is not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:15215 | Other sentencing principles
-- src:15216 | 718.2 A court that imposes a sentence shall also take into consideration the following principles:
@ref s 718.2 (src:15215-15216)
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2 requires the court to take the principles into consideration` MEANS
    IF `the court imposes a sentence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that imposes a sentence shall also take into consideration the following principles"

-- (a): the circumstances that "shall be deemed to be aggravating circumstances". Limb (viii) turns on a date test and has its own function below.
-- src:15217 | (a) a sentence should be increased or reduced to account for any relevant aggravating or mitigating circumstances relating to the offence or the offender, and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:15218 | (i) evidence that the offence was motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on race, national or ethnic origin, language, colour, religion, sex, age, mental or physical disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity or expression, or on any other similar factor,
-- src:15219 | (ii) evidence that the offender, in committing the offence, abused the offender’s intimate partner or a member of the victim or the offender’s family,
-- src:15220 | (ii.1) evidence that the offender, in committing the offence, abused a person under the age of eighteen years,
-- src:15221 | (ii.2) evidence that the offender counselled or otherwise involved a person under the age of 18 years in the commission of the offence,
-- src:15222 | (iii) evidence that the offender, in committing the offence, abused a position of trust or authority in relation to the victim,
-- src:15223 | (iii.1) evidence that the offence had a significant impact on the victim, considering their age and other personal circumstances, including their health and financial situation,
-- src:15224 | (iii.2) evidence that the offence was committed against a person who, in the performance of their duties and functions, was providing health services, including personal care services, or was providing services as a first responder,
-- src:15225 | (iv) evidence that the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization,
-- src:15226 | (v) evidence that the offence was a terrorism offence,
-- src:15227 | (vi) evidence that the offence was committed while the offender was subject to a conditional sentence order made under section 742.1 or released on parole, statutory release or unescorted temporary absence under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act,
-- src:15228 | (vii) evidence that the commission of the offence had the effect of impeding another person from obtaining health services, including personal care services, and
@ref s 718.2(a) (src:15217-15228)
DECLARE `s 718.2(a) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 718.2(a)(i) the offence was motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on race, national or ethnic origin, language, colour, religion, sex, age, mental or physical disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other similar factor`
    `s 718.2(a)(ii) the offender abused the offender's intimate partner or a member of the victim's or the offender's family`
    `s 718.2(a)(ii.1) the offender abused a person under the age of eighteen years`
    `s 718.2(a)(ii.2) the offender counselled or otherwise involved a person under the age of 18 years in the commission of the offence`
    `s 718.2(a)(iii) the offender abused a position of trust or authority in relation to the victim`
    `s 718.2(a)(iii.1) the offence had a significant impact on the victim, considering their age and other personal circumstances`
    `s 718.2(a)(iii.2) the offence was committed against a person providing health services or services as a first responder in the performance of their duties`
    `s 718.2(a)(iv) the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`
    `s 718.2(a)(v) the offence was a terrorism offence`
    `s 718.2(a)(vi) the offence was committed while the offender was subject to a conditional sentence order or released on parole, statutory release or unescorted temporary absence`
    `s 718.2(a)(vii) the commission of the offence had the effect of impeding another person from obtaining health services`
    `s 718.2(a) another circumstance relating to the offence or the offender`

@ref s 718.2(a) (src:15217-15228)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 718.2(a) circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(i) the offence was motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on race, national or ethnic origin, language, colour, religion, sex, age, mental or physical disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other similar factor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(ii) the offender abused the offender's intimate partner or a member of the victim's or the offender's family` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(ii.1) the offender abused a person under the age of eighteen years` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(ii.2) the offender counselled or otherwise involved a person under the age of 18 years in the commission of the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(iii) the offender abused a position of trust or authority in relation to the victim` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(iii.1) the offence had a significant impact on the victim, considering their age and other personal circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(iii.2) the offence was committed against a person providing health services or services as a first responder in the performance of their duties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(iv) the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(v) the offence was a terrorism offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(vi) the offence was committed while the offender was subject to a conditional sentence order or released on parole, statutory release or unescorted temporary absence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a)(vii) the commission of the offence had the effect of impeding another person from obtaining health services` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.2(a) another circumstance relating to the offence or the offender` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "without limiting the generality of the foregoing"

-- (a)(viii): violence, threats or attempts of violence AND a conviction, within the previous five years, of one or more such offences.
-- Reference point of "within the previous five years": the day the sentence is imposed (fork); a conviction on the day five years back counts (fork).
-- src:15229 | (viii) evidence that the offence was committed with the use of violence, threats or attempts of violence against another person and that the offender has been convicted, within the previous five years, of one or more such offences,
-- src:15230 | shall be deemed to be aggravating circumstances;
@ref s 718.2(a)(viii) (src:15229-15230)
GIVEN `the offence was committed with the use of violence, threats or attempts of violence against another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has been convicted of one or more such offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the offender's most recent conviction for such an offence` IS A DATE
      `the date the sentence is imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(a)(viii) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` MEANS
    IF     `the offence was committed with the use of violence, threats or attempts of violence against another person`
       AND `the offender has been convicted of one or more such offences`
       AND `s 716 the earlier date falls within the five years up to and including the later date` `the date of the offender's most recent conviction for such an offence` `the date the sentence is imposed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "convicted, within the previous five years, of one or more such offences"

-- (a), first words: "a sentence should be increased or reduced to account for any relevant aggravating or mitigating circumstances".
-- src:15217 | (a) a sentence should be increased or reduced to account for any relevant aggravating or mitigating circumstances relating to the offence or the offender, and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
@ref s 718.2(a) (src:15217)
GIVEN `there is a relevant aggravating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(a) the sentence should be increased` MEANS
    IF `there is a relevant aggravating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a sentence should be increased or reduced to account for any relevant aggravating or mitigating circumstances"

@ref s 718.2(a) (src:15217)
GIVEN `there is a relevant mitigating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(a) the sentence should be reduced` MEANS
    IF `there is a relevant mitigating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a sentence should be increased or reduced to account for any relevant aggravating or mitigating circumstances"

-- src:15231 | (b) a sentence should be similar to sentences imposed on similar offenders for similar offences committed in similar circumstances;
@ref s 718.2(b) (src:15231)
GIVEN `the sentence is similar to sentences imposed on similar offenders for similar offences committed in similar circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(b) the sentence meets the principle of parity` MEANS
    IF `the sentence is similar to sentences imposed on similar offenders for similar offences committed in similar circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a sentence should be similar to sentences imposed on similar offenders for similar offences committed in similar circumstances"

-- (c): a bar. "where consecutive sentences are imposed, the combined sentence should not be unduly long or harsh".
-- src:15232 | (c) where consecutive sentences are imposed, the combined sentence should not be unduly long or harsh;
@ref s 718.2(c) (src:15232)
GIVEN `consecutive sentences are imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the combined sentence is unduly long or harsh` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(c) the combined sentence is barred as unduly long or harsh` MEANS
    IF `consecutive sentences are imposed` AND `the combined sentence is unduly long or harsh`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where consecutive sentences are imposed, the combined sentence should not be unduly long or harsh"

-- (d): a bar. "an offender should not be deprived of liberty, if less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances".
-- src:15233 | (d) an offender should not be deprived of liberty, if less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances; and
@ref s 718.2(d) (src:15233)
GIVEN `less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(d) deprivation of liberty is barred` MEANS
    IF `less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances"

-- (e): "all available sanctions, other than imprisonment, that are reasonable in the circumstances and consistent with the harm done to victims
-- or to the community should be considered for all offenders, with particular attention to the circumstances of Aboriginal offenders".
-- src:15234 | (e) all available sanctions, other than imprisonment, that are reasonable in the circumstances and consistent with the harm done to victims or to the community should be considered for all offenders, with particular attention to the circumstances of Aboriginal offenders.
@ref s 718.2(e) (src:15234)
GIVEN `the sanction is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanction is imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanction is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanction is consistent with the harm done to victims or to the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(e) the sanction should be considered` MEANS
    IF     `the sanction is available`
       AND (NOT `the sanction is imprisonment`)
       AND `the sanction is reasonable in the circumstances`
       AND `the sanction is consistent with the harm done to victims or to the community`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all available sanctions, other than imprisonment, that are reasonable in the circumstances and consistent with the harm done to victims or to the community should be considered"

@ref s 718.2(e) (src:15234)
GIVEN `the offender is Aboriginal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.2(e) particular attention is due to the circumstances of the offender` MEANS
    IF `the offender is Aboriginal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with particular attention to the circumstances of Aboriginal offenders"

§ `Section 718.201 -- Additional consideration: increased vulnerability`

-- src:15235 | Additional consideration — increased vulnerability
-- src:15236 | 718.201 A court that imposes a sentence in respect of an offence that involved the abuse of an intimate partner shall consider the increased vulnerability of female persons who are victims, giving particular attention to the circumstances of Aboriginal female victims.
@ref s 718.201 (src:15235-15236)
GIVEN `the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.201 requires the court to consider the increased vulnerability of female victims` MEANS
    IF `the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that imposes a sentence in respect of an offence that involved the abuse of an intimate partner shall consider the increased vulnerability of female persons who are victims"

@ref s 718.201 (src:15235-15236)
GIVEN `the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is Aboriginal and female` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.201 particular attention is due to the circumstances of the victim` MEANS
    IF `the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner` AND `the victim is Aboriginal and female`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "giving particular attention to the circumstances of Aboriginal female victims"

§ `Section 718.21 -- Organizations: additional factors`

-- src:15238 | Organizations
-- src:15239 | Additional factors
-- src:15240 | 718.21 A court that imposes a sentence on an organization shall also take into consideration the following factors:
-- src:15241 | (a) any advantage realized by the organization as a result of the offence;
-- src:15242 | (b) the degree of planning involved in carrying out the offence and the duration and complexity of the offence;
-- src:15243 | (c) whether the organization has attempted to conceal its assets, or convert them, in order to show that it is not able to pay a fine or make restitution;
-- src:15244 | (d) the impact that the sentence would have on the economic viability of the organization and the continued employment of its employees;
-- src:15245 | (e) the cost to public authorities of the investigation and prosecution of the offence;
-- src:15246 | (f) any regulatory penalty imposed on the organization or one of its representatives in respect of the conduct that formed the basis of the offence;
-- src:15247 | (g) whether the organization was — or any of its representatives who were involved in the commission of the offence were — convicted of a similar offence or sanctioned by a regulatory body for similar conduct;
-- src:15248 | (h) any penalty imposed by the organization on a representative for their role in the commission of the offence;
-- src:15249 | (i) any restitution that the organization is ordered to make or any amount that the organization has paid to a victim of the offence; and
-- src:15250 | (j) any measures that the organization has taken to reduce the likelihood of it committing a subsequent offence.
@ref s 718.21 (src:15238-15250)
DECLARE `s 718.21 factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 718.21(a) any advantage realized by the organization as a result of the offence`
    `s 718.21(b) the degree of planning involved in carrying out the offence and the duration and complexity of the offence`
    `s 718.21(c) whether the organization has attempted to conceal its assets, or convert them, in order to show that it is not able to pay a fine or make restitution`
    `s 718.21(d) the impact that the sentence would have on the economic viability of the organization and the continued employment of its employees`
    `s 718.21(e) the cost to public authorities of the investigation and prosecution of the offence`
    `s 718.21(f) any regulatory penalty imposed on the organization or one of its representatives in respect of the conduct that formed the basis of the offence`
    `s 718.21(g) whether the organization, or any of its representatives who were involved in the commission of the offence, were convicted of a similar offence or sanctioned by a regulatory body for similar conduct`
    `s 718.21(h) any penalty imposed by the organization on a representative for their role in the commission of the offence`
    `s 718.21(i) any restitution that the organization is ordered to make or any amount that the organization has paid to a victim of the offence`
    `s 718.21(j) any measures that the organization has taken to reduce the likelihood of it committing a subsequent offence`
    `s 718.21 another factor`

@ref s 718.21 (src:15238-15250)
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence on an organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 718.21 factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court imposes a sentence on an organization` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that imposes a sentence on an organization shall also take into consideration the following factors"
        IF factor EQUALS `s 718.21 another factor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following factors"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
